  "lore": "Born of the primordial \"smokeless fire,\" the Djinni is a creature of sublime and terrifying majesty. They frequent the trackless reaches of the Great Erg, where the veil between our world and the celestial firmament thins. To the unwary, the Djinni does not hunt with claw or fang, but through the architecture of desire. They are predators of the spirit, weaving intricate mirages\u2014glimmering oases or spired citadels\u2014to lure travelers into ruinous bargains. They feast not on meat, but on the hubris and desperation of those who dare entreat them.\n\nIn local lore, the Djinn are whispered of as \"The Architects of the Simoom.\" Nomads claim the shifting dunes are merely the hem of their silken robes as they stride across the wastes. To meet one is to stand before a storm given voice; they are neither inherently malevolent nor kind, but possess a morality as mercurial as the winds they command. One must approach with a silver tongue and a guarded heart, for a Djinni\u2019s favor is a gilded cage, and their wrath is a desert sun that never sets.",
